505 1  Ghosts -- Last seen. 
520    Ghosts deals with important art objects which have been 
       damaged, stolen or have otherwise disappeared from public 
       view. Sophie Calle resurrects the memory of these pieces 
       in a series of profiles of each individual work of art.  
       Through language and photography, she explores their 
       personal meaning to those museum employees and others who 
       knew the works intimately.  The first part of Ghosts 
       addresses pieces from the Musée d'Art Moderne, Paris and 
       the Museum of Modern Art, New York, that were out on 
       temporary loan.  The second part, Last seen, addresses 
       pieces stolen in 1990 from the Isabella Stewart Gardner 
       Museum in Boston; a painting partly destroyed by vandalism
       in 1980 from the Musée Cantonal des Beaux-Arts in 
       Lausanne; a Picasso painting Tête stolen in 1994 from 
       Richard Gray Gallery in Chicago; and a Titian painting 
       stolen in 1995 from the Marquis of Bath at Longleat House,
       England. 
